== fuller page ==
Is anyone home? Before a host can do anything else, it has to find out. In
C4's shell library for the ghostwheel, ghostwheel.fn.sh, a run-level that is
not set yet means "startup hasn't finished" [unset]. The first level is 0,
bootstrapping [zero].

At level 0 the library runs only the tests "which can indicate startup
issues" [only0]. They ask plain questions. Are its four names filled in:
C4_ID, C4_ROOT, C4_AS and C4_GW [names]? Is the host it runs on really this
host, by its long name and by its short one, and is "moo" not it [me]? Every
test the file declares today sits at level 0 [count].

Last of all, the library defines a function "to confirm we exist!", which
prints C4 GHOSTWHEEL and a version number [exist]. When you log in, the
start-up file gw.rc loads the library and asks that function to speak. If the
answer begins with C4, someone is home, and only then does it go on to bring
the spokes up [ready].

Notice what the tests do not do: they do not stop the machine. The file's rule
is "Emit warnings about problems; no dying" [nodie]. A host that cannot answer
every question at floor 0 still says what it found, and keeps going.

